1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,000
Watch human approval create the browser's
missing commit tool.

2
00:00:05,000 --> 00:00:07,800
A service coordinator reconciles
vehicle history,

3
00:00:07,800 --> 00:00:12,000
provider qualification, price, availability,
and one consequential final action.

4
00:00:12,000 --> 00:00:15,556
The request requires a certified provider
before Friday,

5
00:00:15,556 --> 00:00:20,000
under sixty thousand yen, with history
reviewed—but no submission.

6
00:00:20,000 --> 00:00:25,000
A deterministic runner invokes five
WebMCP tools—not a simulated AI.

7
00:00:25,000 --> 00:00:27,000
Draft ready; commit absent.

8
00:00:27,000 --> 00:00:31,000
The human approves that exact dispatch.

9
00:00:31,000 --> 00:00:35,000
The actual registry changes
from five tools to six.

10
00:00:35,000 --> 00:00:42,000
Tool zero six is hash-bound, valid for two minutes,
and usable once.

11
00:00:42,000 --> 00:00:48,000
The selected provider meets certification,
budget, availability, and deadline.

12
00:00:48,000 --> 00:00:52,000
Both alternatives keep their exclusion reasons.

13
00:00:52,000 --> 00:00:55,889
Invoke once. The fictional in-memory
action commits;

14
00:00:55,889 --> 00:01:02,000
the result settles, approval is consumed,
and the temporary capability unregisters.

15
00:01:02,000 --> 00:01:04,500
Six becomes five.

16
00:01:04,500 --> 00:01:12,000
The committed result and named revoke
remain visible in the same browser view.

17
00:01:12,000 --> 00:01:20,000
Reset is repeatable and restores
the same five preparation tools.

18
00:01:20,000 --> 00:01:23,900
This is a frozen, fictional browser-local prototype,

19
00:01:23,900 --> 00:01:27,840
not production authorization
or an external business write.

20
00:01:27,840 --> 00:01:34,000
It has no customer data, authenticated approver,
database, or measured outcome.

21
00:01:34,000 --> 00:01:42,000
Five tools prepare, approval creates the sixth,
and one use returns the registry to five.

22
00:01:42,000 --> 00:01:46,267
Evidence stays source-labeled: public-v1 native evidence
and candidate automation.

23
00:01:46,267 --> 00:01:50,000
The final-candidate native gate
is separately recorded.

24
00:01:50,000 --> 00:01:53,818
The pilot hypothesis is
narrower coordination authority.

25
00:01:53,818 --> 00:02:02,000
Measure re-entry, corrections, and exposure duration,
without claiming results this prototype has not produced.

26
00:02:02,000 --> 00:02:10,000
Prepare broadly. Authorize exactly.
Revoke after one use.
